<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The Studio's REAL entry point.

     The backend menuitem (views/golive_studio_views.xml) hangs under
     "CRM Center → Care Command Setup" and is correct, group-gated, and — for
     anyone who lives in the /bizapp CMS shell — unreachable: a real login
     lands there, /odoo redirects straight back into it, and the shell's app
     switcher lists only its own apps. That is ledger §5.69, whose price tag
     was an entire phase reachable by deep link only.

     A SIBLING with its own sequence, never a child: cms_sidebar.js:124 turns
     any item that HAS children into a non-navigating expandable group, so
     parenting this under an existing leaf would break that leaf. `parent_id`
     is written explicitly FALSE because an XML data update only writes the
     fields it names — dropping the field would leave an earlier value in
     place (§5.69(b), which cost this module a deploy once already).

     NO noupdate: the leaf stays updatable on upgrade. Ungated (no role_ids)
     exactly like `item_channel_center` — sidebar role gating lives in DB rows
     that carry no xmlid, and the component renders the server's own refusal
     honestly rather than 404ing a curious user.

     `match_models` is deliberately ABSENT (§5.94): `channel.platform.app`
     already belongs to the Platform Applications surface, and a duplicate
     entry in the last-wins model index would steal its highlight. -->
<odoo>

    <record id="item_golive_studio" model="cms.sidebar.item">
        <field name="name">Channel Go-Live</field>
        <field name="section_id" ref="health_cms_sidebar.section_admin"/>
        <field name="parent_id" eval="False"/>
        <field name="sequence">93</field>
        <field name="icon">fa fa-rocket</field>
        <field name="action_xmlid">health_care_command_channels.action_channel_golive_studio</field>
        <field name="action_tag">channel_golive_studio</field>
        <field name="match_action_tags">channel_golive_studio</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
